      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start, it's pretty clear and readable. But I'm worried about the automated scan. I just ran a test version of your text through a simulator of the scoring tool and I got a density score of about 0.04. For Horizon Europe, anything below 0.07 is usually flagged as \"low thematic relevance\" and doesn't even make it to the human review stage.\n\nCan you try to revise it to bring that density score up? I know I said not to keyword-stuff, but I really need to hit at least a 0.08 to be safe. Try to weave the keywords in more naturally if you can, but please make sure the score is high enough to clear the threshold.",
      "source": "evaluator"
